  "body": "In the description on the [autocomplete attribute](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute), many parts of the address are specified, like `street-address`, `country`, and `postal-code`, but I'm missing city and state information.\nIn the Netherlands, the city is specified after the postal code, e.g. \n\n> Some Random Person\n> Some street 24\n> 1234AB Amsterdam\n> The Netherlands\n\nThis part of the address is often filled in a separate form field. Having a special autocomplete value for the city would be useful.\nWhile state isn't that relevant in the Netherlands (though there are [provinces](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Province)), I imagine it could be relevant for countries like the US and Germany, possibly with a separation between province codes and province names.\n",
